WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.507
Unstructured data does not naturally arrive as a table.

00:00:03.507 --> 00:00:09.042
A clinical note contains useful information, but the meaning is embedded in text.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.922
An image contains visual information.

00:00:11.922 --> 00:00:14.812
Audio contains signals over time.

00:00:14.812 --> 00:00:20.427
To analyze these sources, we usually need an extraction step such as NLP, computer vision, OCR,

00:00:20.427 --> 00:00:21.647
or speech processing.

00:00:21.647 --> 00:00:26.812
After extraction, some information may become structured features that can be analyzed alongside relational

00:00:26.812 --> 00:00:35.957
data. A useful project question is: what preparation step is required before analysis can even begin?

00:00:35.957 --> 00:00:38.467
A relational table may be ready for profiling, JSON may need flattening,

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:41.672
and free text may need NLP or another extraction step.

00:00:41.672 --> 00:00:48.972
The form of the data changes the engineering path, but it does not by itself tell us whether

00:00:48.972 --> 00:00:50.737
the data is high quality.
